  "finalText": "The best-resolution entry is **1AX8**, at **2.4 Å**, solved by **X-ray diffraction**.\n\n1. **UniProtKB:** I searched for the reviewed human LEP entry and found P41159. It cross-references 10 PDB entries: 1AX8, 7Z3Q, 8AVE, 8AVF, 8AVO, 8K6Z, 8X80, 8X81, 8X85 and 9PUO.\n2. **RCSB PDB:** I looked up all 10 entries in RCSB's own data to get each one's resolution and method:\n\n| PDB | Method (RCSB) | Resolution (Å) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1AX8** | **X-ray diffraction** | **2.4** |\n| 9PUO | X-ray diffraction | 3.1 |\n| 8X85 | Electron microscopy | 3.58 |\n| 7Z3Q | X-ray diffraction | 3.617 |\n| 8X81 | Electron microscopy | 3.77 |\n| 8X80 | Electron microscopy | 3.88 |\n| 8AVE | Electron microscopy | 5.62 |\n| 8AVF | Electron microscopy | 6.45 |\n| 8AVO | Electron microscopy | 6.84 |\n| 8K6Z | Solution NMR | none |\n\n8K6Z is a solution NMR structure, so it has no resolution value and was left out of the comparison. UniProt's own figure for 1AX8 (2.40 Å, X-ray) matches RCSB's.\n\nANSWER: 1AX8 | 2.4 | X-ray diffraction"
